---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
const collections = [
  ['Podcasts & conversations', 'Founder interviews and the original recommended podcast collection.', '/resources/podcasts/'],
  ['Regenerating Grassroots videos', 'Six source-described films and conversations, linked to their original platforms.', '/resources/videos/'],
  ['Architects of the Future', 'A creative interview series exploring the futures people are working toward.', '/resources/architects-of-the-future/'],
  ['The Response', 'Community-led responses and mutual aid in the aftermath of disasters.', '/resources/the-response/'],
  ['Seeds of Change', 'The original International Permaculture Convergence video.', '/resources/seeds-of-change/'],
  ['Newsletter archive', 'The foundation’s recovered 2018 and 2019 newsletter issues.', '/resources/newsletters/'],
  ['Youth in Permaculture', 'The prize program, its original resources, and recipient history.', '/youth/'],
  ['Project & grant history', 'Explore the original project records, map, and year-by-year support lists.', '/history/'],
];
---
<Layout title="Learning & resources">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Knowledge is something we share" title="A little understanding. New possibilities." description="Explore the foundation’s conversations, films, newsletters, and the ideas behind regenerative growing." />
  <section class="section container"><div class="feature-grid" style="margin-top:0">{collections.map(([title, description, href]) => <article class="feature-card"><h2 style="font-size:1.8rem;margin-bottom:16px">{title}</h2><p>{description}</p><a class="text-link" href={href}>Explore the collection <Icon /></a></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="section container article-grid" style="padding-top:0"><div class="prose"><h2>What is permaculture?</h2><p>Permaculture is an approach to designing human systems with lessons from nature. It connects care for the Earth, care for people, and responsible sharing of resources. A garden is one expression of it; community organization, water use, and learning can be others.</p><h2>What is agroforestry?</h2><p>Agroforestry brings trees together with crops or other agricultural activities. A diverse planting can support food production, soil health, habitat, and resilience when it is designed for local conditions.</p><h2>What is a food forest?</h2><p>A food forest grows food using a woodland-like structure: different plants occupy different layers and roles. It may combine fruit trees, shrubs, herbs, and ground-cover plants.</p><h2>What makes an approach regenerative?</h2><p>Regenerative approaches aim to renew the health of living systems: soils, biodiversity, water, and the relationships that communities depend on. Outcomes depend on place, practice, and sustained care.</p><h2>Original editorial resources</h2><p>The original blog articles have not been transferred. These links remain on the original publisher’s website:</p><ul><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/articles/biomimicry/">Biomimicry</a></li><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/articles/resilience/">Resilience</a></li><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/articles/bee-the-change/">Bee the Change</a></li><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/larrykorn/">Remembering Larry Korn</a></li></ul></div><aside class="aside-card"><h2>Put ideas into practice.</h2><p>Find work happening in communities and opportunities to contribute your skills.</p><a class="button" href="/projects/">Explore projects <Icon /></a><a class="text-link" href="/internships/">Internship opportunities <Icon /></a></aside></section>
  <Newsletter />
</Layout>
